From c2c64c1ad3ee84f1cdb6f9b88aeb87bbf3438baa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:27:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(printing): add printer configuration and a print
 endpoint

Adds a 'printer' table plus CRUD under /api/v1/printer, so a Spoolman
instance can be pointed at a label printer once and print to it directly.

- GET /printer/discover lists the queues a CUPS server offers, so a printer
  that already exists on the host can be picked instead of typed in.
- POST /printer/{id}/test reports reachability. A printer that is off is a
  valid answer, not a server error, so it still responds 200.
- POST /printer/{id}/print submits an already-rendered document. Size is
  checked before decoding the base64 so an oversized payload is rejected
  without being expanded in memory first.

Purely additive: one router registration, one model appended, one migration.
No existing behaviour changes, and nothing happens for users who never
configure a printer.

tests/test_ipp_live.py exercises the client against a real IPP server when
SPOOLMAN_TEST_IPP_HOST is set, and is skipped otherwise.
